From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <luke@agent54.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/50] direct route: adaptive pipelining depth by default, measured on single copies, with hysteresis

The default was a fixed depth of 2 (one copy delivered plus one parked in
viz). At N = 32 that gave 30-37 ms latency after stage G (15 ms in five of
six runs before); a fixed depth of 1 gives 15 ms but halves throughput at
N = 64 (17.3 vs 32.1 fps per page).

pipelineDepth now defaults to 0 (adaptive). The estimate uses only copies
issued while no other copy was pending (a copy queued behind another
measures the queue, not the path); going deeper needs the smoothed round
trip to exceed each two-frame step by 4 ms, coming back needs it 4 ms
below; a deeper depth is held 2 s, then depth 1 is probed with four
single-copy samples, and a failed probe doubles the hold (up to 16 s).

Release, Wayland, 640x360 guests, 3 runs: N = 16 58.0 fps/page, latency
8 ms (one run 24 ms); N = 32 57.7, 15 ms; N = 64 28.8, 72 ms; 8 of 64
animating 58.0, 6 ms. (Fixed depth 2: 57.9 / 59.7 / 32.1 fps, 8 / 30 /
66 ms.)
---
